 "text": "On 6 hours of sleep, you feel fine, you're not. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 19. Dev wants to ship his app, he codes from 11 till 1. Week 1 feels great, week 3 the same 2 hours finish almost nothing and he decides he's not good at this. Sleep researchers found that on 6 hours a night, people got worse at attention tests nearly every day but felt only a little sleepy. So Dev stopped borrowing from sleep, lights out at 1130, and he moved the code to the time before work when he's sharp. Fewer hours more finished and this time he didn't quit. Send this to the friend who's coding at 1 am. That's what Demure is for, archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day, tonight caber and the day that was okay. What time do you actually fall asleep, the link's in the bio.",
